/-! ## `thm:groundreads`(v)'s Euclidean brackets at two committed
gaps, the count tier and the growth chain.

The order-one gap `Et = [2]` is diagonalized by the congruence `[1]`
at its one root `2` on the gram's `1`.  Its witness list `[(2, 1)]`
reads the positive arm at the coupling `un = ud = 1`, the count
`n = 2` (so `N = 3`) and the cap `[2 : 1]`: the gap identity
`1 · 2 + 1 = 3 · (1 · 1)` and the cap `2 · 1 ≤ 2 · 1`.  Its two
solved witnesses are `L = [1]` at the clearing `lc = 3`
(`3 · 1 + 3 · 2 = 9 = 3 · 3`) and `V = [3]` at `vc = 5`
(`3 · 3 + 2 · 3 = 15 = 3 · 5`).

The order-two gap `Et = diag(0, 2)` at the identity congruence
carries a kernel root beside a positive one, its witness list
`[(1, 3), (2, 1)]` reading the kernel arm at the full gap
`3 = 3 · (1 · 1)` and the positive arm at the order-one gap's own
data; its witnesses are `L = diag(3, 1)` at `lc = 3` and
`V = diag(15, 9)` at `vc = 15`.  The witnesses' third powers carry
the congruated diagonals `(3375, 729)` and `(27, 1)`, so the bracket
`lc³ · dsV − vc³ · dsL` reads the sum's unit at the kernel root — the
tight cell — and `16308` at the positive root, the width display
`16308 · 3 = 48924` against `4 · 45³ = 364500` at the gram scale's
own unit.

The column reads land at both witnesses: the lower column at the
order-one gap through `euc_lo_col` at the positive arm and at the
order-two gap through `euc_lo_col_ker` at the kernel arm, the upper
column through `euc_hi_col` with its per-root arm disjunction derived
from `eucRead_arm`.  The pair-of-families price closes the witness
tier at the order-one gap, the probes `x = [1]` and `y = [2]` at unit
weights reading `7248 ≤ 67500`.

The certificate's three binders refuse one at a time: the cap at
`kn = 1`, where the root's representative `2` sits beyond `1 · 1`;
the gap identity at the witness `(2, 2)`, reading `4` against `3`;
and the arm at the gap `[-2]`, its own diagonal read standing, where
